---
globs: *.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use the App Router for better performance and organization of routes.
- Implement proper error boundaries to handle errors gracefully.
- Optimize data fetching with `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps` as needed.
- Utilize dynamic routing for cleaner URL structures.

---

name: typescript-best-practices.mdc
description: TypeScript coding standards and type safety guidelines
globs: \*_/_.{ts,tsx}

---

- Enable strict mode in `tsconfig.json` for better type safety.
- Prefer using interfaces over type aliases for object shapes.
- Use type guards to ensure type safety in conditional logic.
- Leverage generics for reusable components and functions.

---

name: supabase-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for using Supabase in applications
globs: \*_/_.{ts,tsx}

---

- Use environment variables to manage Supabase keys securely.
- Implement real-time subscriptions for data updates.
- Structure database tables and relationships for optimal querying.
- Use Supabase's built-in authentication for user management.

---

name: playwright-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for testing with Playwright
globs: \*_/_.spec.{ts,js}

---

- Organize tests into unit, integration, and end-to-end categories.
- Use fixtures to set up test data and state.
- Implement parallel test execution to speed up testing.
- Utilize Playwright's built-in tracing for debugging flaky tests.

---

name: eslint-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for ESLint configuration and usage
globs: \*_/_.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}

---

- Use `eslint-config-next` for Next.js specific linting rules.
- Enable `--fix` option in scripts to automatically fix linting issues.
- Regularly update ESLint and plugins to leverage new features.
- Customize rules based on team preferences and project needs.

---

name: openapi-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for working with OpenAPI specifications
globs: \*_/_.yaml

---

- Keep OpenAPI specifications up-to-date with code changes.
- Use tools like `openapi-generator-cli` for generating client libraries.
- Validate OpenAPI specs using `swagger-parser` before deployment.
- Document all endpoints clearly for better API usability.
